<code>assert CollectionUtils.isEqualCollection(coll, this);</code>

However, since we need to use only publicly accessible observer methods provided in the test function and avoid calling the constructor directly, we should use the `size()` and `get(int index)` methods to compare the contents. Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert coll.size() == this.size() && \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < coll.size(); coll.contains(this.get(i));</code>

This ensures that the constructed `TreeList` has the same size and contains the same elements as the input collection.
